<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Trips</span>
<h1>Hanoi to Cat Ba by Motorbike: Choosing a Bike for the Trip</h1>
<p>Cat Ba asks a machine for three different days in one, endurance on the long flat corridor east, composure in the ferry&rsquo;s queue and crossing, and manners on an island&rsquo;s slow shared roads, and the classes that answer all three are the ones this guide chooses honestly. It quotes only the shop&rsquo;s verified daily classes and invents nothing about range, top speed or model years, because the honest answers about a specific machine live at the desk, on the day, and the island adds parking as a fourth question the mainland trips never ask.</p>
<p>The machine you choose can come from Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily 09:00 to 21:00, where the desk pairs riders and island routes every day and keeps its honest opinions until asked. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/">Hanoi motorbike trips</a> hub, study the parent <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-trips/long-distance-motorbike-trip-planning/">long-distance motorbike trip planning</a> guide, see the machines and terms on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> page, review the <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a> for riding and safety, and keep <a href="/renting-a-motorbike-in-vietnam/">renting a motorbike in Vietnam</a> open for the legal layer.</p>
